   "text": {
    "L1": "An angle is classified by its measure, not by how it is turned on the page.",
    "L2": "A tilted right angle is still a right angle because its measure is exactly 90 degrees.",
    "L3": "Acute angles are more than 0 degrees and less than 90 degrees. Right angles are exactly 90 degrees.",
    "L4": "Obtuse angles are more than 90 degrees and less than 180 degrees. A straight angle is exactly 180 degrees.",
    "L5": "A straight angle is two rays from one vertex pointing in opposite directions.",
    "L6": "A reflex angle is more than 180 degrees and less than 360 degrees; it is the outside part of an angle in a full turn.",
    "L7": "For the worked example, 25 degrees is acute, 90 degrees is right, and 145 degrees is obtuse.",
    "L8": "Also, 180 degrees is straight and 300 degrees is reflex. Now classify 145 degrees."
   },
